part e1_owns
  tally 1
  note "A counts what Ania and Tomek are worth over every place of the reality, by owns (A/worth.tally:39–45; L §5.9: by kind or owner, never by a hand-kept list). In the family the built-in index place also holds B's and D's places, and a sum whose where is a hole is a hole (L §5.10, aggregates), so each spouse's share of them is stated: none (O:E1-2). Outside places need no row: kind(x) != outside stops the and (L §5.10, logic)."

version e1_owns_b
  cite e1_story
  known 2021-01-01
  note "B's places with no key that are not outside (B/places.tally): Piotr's, Ola's, or theirs together"
